    "brsup.lead": "Everything you need to know about Homemade Breathing. If your question isn't answered here, just email us — we read every message.",
    "brsup.q1": "Which technique should I start with?",
    "brsup.a1": "Coherent at the Standard level: five seconds in, five out, no holds. It is the best-studied rhythm and the default. For a stressful moment try Sigh, for winding down at night Relaxing 4-7-8 (or Calm if holds feel hard), and before something demanding, Box. Options → Compare the techniques explains each one.",
    "brsup.q2": "I feel dizzy or light-headed.",
    "brsup.a2": "Stop and breathe normally — breathing should always feel easy. Next time choose the Gentle level, or a technique without holds such as Coherent or Calm. If you are pregnant, have a heart or lung condition or get panic attacks, prefer the patterns without holds and ask a doctor if unsure.",
